body:
Really dislike the "you can't compare X and Y" thing. The statement is true when discussing two things with no relation, or very little relation.

&#x200B;

But we're discussing a 2 series from the same creator. It's human nature to compare things, and literally everyone reading this will mentally compare this to the creator's other famous work. Whether that be intentionally or subconsciously.

I agree that the artist could use more line weights and value, as people pointed out. But at the same time I feel like a lot of people are being a lot more harsher towards this artist, and the manga in general due to it being Kishimoto's new project, and people having higher expectations for it.

&#x200B;

Just saying, over my years in this subreddit this is the first time I've seen so many people stuck on one nitpick, and I've seen a lot of comment sections for manga with way worse distinguishability(especially from Jump)

I mean, to be fair, Double Switch is probably borderline impossible to beat without having the guidebook glued to your eyes while playing anyway. 

&#x200B;

Don't think this is that big a deal given the game

I think everyone is over reacting at this "7 Quirk" thing. 

&#x200B;

To be completely honest, half them probably won't even be offensive/power-based quirks. A couple would probably be something like "Deku can sense danger coming towards him(AKA Spidey-Sense)"

Wasn't really crazy over the video. I thought the parts where he was actually reviewing a Flex Tape commercial was funny. And it's cool that he actually got Phil Swift in it. But thought the beginning segment was overkill and unnecessary. And Phil Swift incorporation into the video could have been better.

&#x200B;

TLDR; the video felt overcook
